, \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIMQNvvCya66a6YyDlxwkxjjJPN3uaFI+QD3OjyC8e1UF rebar-mac-492a5c71 joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com 20261119"},{"content_hash":"d0e3731fd3aed508aa0706989fabae50d977c8d4bfd95909b4adcf2bc22ec784","event_uuid":"8c3322ba-7c89-451f-a690-d81bd2fbe357","position":{"commit_sha":"aa4521fe7b6a18c7f9991eef47c258259270bf98","position":"1795275141987327001-8c3322ba-7c89-451f-a690-d81bd2fbe357"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIMQNvvCya66a6YyDlxwkxjjJPN3uaFI+QD3OjyC8e1UF rebar-mac-492a5c71 joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com 20261119"},{"content_hash":"c0f2c0a9ce17a7fc430748dc2a9a75dae893d8ebf91e7dee2850e9e93865495b","event_uuid":"2bdc2233-ec8d-45a4-89eb-5cb5a0e6e25a","position":{"commit_sha":"aa4521fe7b6a18c7f9991eef47c258259270bf98","position":"1795275152313925001-2bdc2233-ec8d-45a4-89eb-5cb5a0e6e25a"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIMQNvvCya66a6YyDlxwkxjjJPN3uaFI+QD3OjyC8e1UF rebar-mac-492a5c71 joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com 20261119"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-311_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"05f74084-8156-4489-b43f-fbb9222cdc20","comments":[],"created_at":1795274372652919001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"5b1ccf40-fe90-4b4a-a13f-e50f135ff7ff","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"10c6-8881-c05e-4209"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nThe Windows sweep on main (run 44911386034, job 136867764314, at a99339e8ce8) failed 2 tests and nothing else (20480 passed): `tests/unit/metrics/test_git_metrics.py::test_history_walk_cat_file_starts_do_not_grow_with_revisions` and `::test_oracle_cap_change_events_compares_unsampled_adjacent_revisions`, both `CalledProcessError: ['git', 'fast-import', '--quiet', '--export-marks=C:\\\\...\\\\repo.marks'] returned non-zero exit status 128`. Both use `_fast_import_history`, added by 863abe7cd19 (rubbery-adamantine-panda). This resets the 3-green-sweep count for charitable-tyrannical-hydra and sporting-feudalist-bluet.\n\n## Root cause (verified)\n`_fast_import_history` passes the fast-import stream with `text=True`. On Windows, Python's text-mode stdin translates every `\\n` to `\\r\\n`. fast-import is line-oriented and byte-counted, so it reads `commit refs/heads/main\\r` and exits 128 (the `data <n>` counts are also off by one per line). The marks path is not the cause.\n\nReproduction on macOS (Nov 21 2026): the same minimal stream fed with LF endings imports (rc 0); with each line ending converted to CRLF, `git fast-import` fails with `fatal: branch name doesn't conform to Git standards: refs/heads/main?` and writes a crash report.\n\n## Approach\nIn `tests/unit/metrics/test_git_metrics.py`, `_fast_import_history` builds the stream as UTF-8 bytes and calls `subprocess.run` without `text=True` (`input=stream.encode(\"utf-8\")`), with `data` counts taken from the encoded byte lengths as before. No newline translation then happens on any platform. No skip: fast-import is cross-platform.\n\n## Scope\n- `tests/unit/metrics/test_git_metrics.py`\n\n## Testing\n- A unit test feeds `_fast_import_history`'s exact stream through a CRLF translation check: it monkeypatches `subprocess.run` to capture `input` and asserts it is `bytes` containing no `\\r`.\n- The 2 failing tests pass on macOS and in a Windows sweep dispatched on a temp branch (`gh workflow run 294845723 --ref tmp/...`), run recorded here, branch deleted afterwards.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The 2 tests pass in a Windows sweep dispatched on the change, recorded here.\n- [ ] A test pins that the fast-import stream is sent as bytes with LF line endings.\n- [ ] `make verify` passes and Gerrit gives Verified +1.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/unit/metrics/test_git_metrics.py","reason":"send the fast-import stream as bytes"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"8c3322ba-7c89-451f-a690-d81bd2fbe357","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"7b3a-e9a8-a547-4ad6","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Windows sweep: metrics fast-import fixture sends its stream in text mode, so Windows writes CRLF and git fast-import exits 128","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["cf2c0d9f-cef9-4c44-a9a6-615c746852ba","5b1ccf40-fe90-4b4a-a13f-e50f135ff7ff","0daaeb30-c6f6-4411-a763-79f196401828","0fbcb837-ce07-482e-a0ec-ab0aa4651afb","8c3322ba-7c89-451f-a690-d81bd2fbe357","2bdc2233-ec8d-45a4-89eb-5cb5a0e6e25a"]},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1795275152313925002,"uuid":"187e137c-b433-472a-9f30-b2fae90f3337"}